# Live WordPress

Use when Matt asks to add/fix **content** on https://acreline.matthummel.com/ — not when the task is theme-only.

## What the live site is

- Live demo: https://acreline.matthummel.com/ (admin user `matthummel`). Theme slug `acreline`. Connected via WPVibe (`vibe-ai`).
- Content is already seeded: Home `#12`, marketing pages, 8 listings, 3 agents, 3 posts. Front page = page 12, posts page = Blog.
- Installing a new theme zip does **not** recreate posts. Missing fields → empty headings unless Blade has `?:` fallbacks.
- Theme updates: CI publishes `theme-latest` on GitHub; install via **Appearance → Update Theme**, or a one-shot WPCode snippet if Matt set one up. Do not assume a merged PR is live until the zip is installed.

## Writes (WPVibe)

- `run_wp_cli` is an emulator, not real WP-CLI. Run **one** command. No `&&`, pipes, or `eval` / `eval-file`.
- `post meta update <id> <key> <value>` — one key per call. Keys are `ks_*`.
- `post update` does **not** support `--meta_input`.
- REST `POST /wp/v2/listing/{id}` ignores unregistered `meta`. Use CLI meta updates.
- Avoid `&` in CLI strings when a write fails (site title, Unsplash query strings). Use `and` or a URL without query params.
- Quote any value that contains spaces (`post update 26 --post_title="Ridge Road Brick Farmhouse"`). Unquoted titles/addresses truncate at the first space. Prefer REST `POST /wp/v2/listing/{id}` for titles.
- `post delete` without `--force` trash is fine; `--force` needs browser approval.
- Do not install plugins unless Matt asks.

## After content writes

The host nginx proxy (`x-proxy-cache`) often keeps a stale `/`. Inner URLs (`/listings/`, `/book/`) usually miss. Confirm with `/?fresh=1` or ask Matt to purge Site Tools → Speed → Caching. `wp cache purge` only clears the WP object cache, not that proxy.

## Local vs live

Local throwaway install: `bin/setup-wp.sh` then `wp server --path="$HOME/wp" --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8080 --allow-root` (admin / admin123). Theme is symlinked from this repo.
